@host = 127.0.0.1
@port = 55681
@token = subconscious-dev-token

# When started with --dev, the engine always listens on 127.0.0.1:55681 and accepts the
# development-only token above. Non-dev runs still publish their dynamic port and random token
# in runtime.json, e.g.:
#   %APPDATA%\Subconscious\runtime.json        (Windows, non-dev)
#   %APPDATA%\Subconscious-dev\runtime.json     (Windows, --dev)
#
# Every route below is mapped in Subconscious.Engine/Api/EngineApi.cs (MapWorkspaceEndpoints) and
# served by WorkspaceService. Bodies and responses are camelCase: minimal APIs use ASP.NET Core's
# JsonSerializerDefaults.Web and the engine configures nothing on top of it. Note that the
# WebSocket frames on /api/v1/events use snake_case instead — the two transports differ.
#
# Everything except /api/v1/health is behind BearerTokenMiddleware; a wrong token is a 401.

### Get all workspaces — 200, ordered by name
GET http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/v1/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one workspace — 200, or 404 if the uuid is unknown
@workspaceUuid = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceUuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a workspace — 200 (not 201) with the created WorkspaceDto.
# Creates the "default" network on the fly if the database has none.
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/v1/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Scratch",
  "description": "Created from workspaces.http",
  "defaultModelId": null
}

### Update a workspace — 200, or 404 if the uuid is unknown.
# Takes the same body as create, and applies it wholesale: omitting "description" sets it to null
# rather than leaving it alone.
PUT http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceUuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Scratch (renamed)",
  "description": "Updated from workspaces.http",
  "defaultModelId": null
}

### Delete a workspace — 204, or 404 if the uuid is unknown.
# Cascades: threads, messages, todos, notes, contacts, memories and indexed documents all go too.
DELETE http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceUuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Threads in a workspace — 200. An unknown uuid is an empty list, not a 404.
GET http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceUuid}}/threads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
